WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:13.248
The school next joins toxidrome recognition with acute kidney injury. We will connect the visible pattern to the immediate threat, then explain why poisoning, heat and poor perfusion can injure several systems together.
学校接下来把中毒综合征识别与急性肾损伤连接起来。本课先把可见模式连到即时威胁，再解释中毒、热及低灌注为何可同时伤及多个系统。

00:00:13.248 --> 00:00:24.024
A toxidrome helps organize findings when the agent is uncertain. It does not replace glucose, neurological assessment, trauma checks or effective basic support.
药物不明时，中毒综合征有助整理发现，但不能替代血糖、神经评估、创伤核查或有效基础支持。

00:00:24.024 --> 00:00:36.480
For renal illness, think about incoming perfusion, injury within the kidney and outgoing urine drainage. The mechanisms may overlap and do not all call for the same fluid treatment.
肾脏问题需分别思考进入的灌注、肾内损伤及离开的尿液引流。机制可能重叠，并非都适合同一种补液处理。

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:49.032
Use these original cases to rehearse an explanation and a next action. The named school sections remain the spine, with the Nancy reading and current local authorization kept visible.
用这些原创病例练习解释及下一步行动。主线仍是学校点名章节，并明确连接Nancy阅读和现行当地授权。

00:00:49.032 --> 00:01:01.512
The same substance can produce different findings depending on the route, time course, formulation and patient. A sustained-release preparation can behave differently from an immediate-release tablet.
同一种物质可因途径、病程、剂型和患者不同而呈现不同发现；缓释制剂的过程可能与速释片不同。

00:01:01.512 --> 00:01:12.360
Absorption may still be occurring when you arrive. A patient who initially talks normally can deteriorate later, so a single comfortable appearance cannot establish safety.
到达时可能仍在吸收。起初能正常交谈者之后仍会恶化，因此一次看似舒适不能证明安全。

00:01:12.360 --> 00:01:25.440
Co-exposures and prescribed medicines can blur a classic pattern. Ask about alcohol, sedating medicines and other agents without assuming that a reported substance is the only one present.
共同暴露及处方药可模糊典型模式。应不作预断地问酒精、镇静药和其他物质，不能认定自述物质就是全部。

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:37.128
Record the reported amount and its uncertainty. A street tablet or a hit is not a standardized concentration, so a unit count does not establish a reliable dose.
记录自述用量及其不确定性。街头药片或“一次”的浓度并不标准，数量不能直接确定可靠剂量。

00:01:37.128 --> 00:01:49.848
Both sympathetic and parasympathetic preganglionic neurons use acetylcholine at nicotinic receptors in autonomic ganglia. Acetylcholine is not limited to the parasympathetic branch.
交感和副交感节前神经元，都在自主神经节的烟碱型受体使用乙酰胆碱；乙酰胆碱并不只属于副交感。

00:01:49.848 --> 00:02:02.904
Most parasympathetic target effects use muscarinic receptors. Most sympathetic target nerves release norepinephrine, while sympathetic sweating pathways use acetylcholine at muscarinic receptors.
大部分副交感靶器官效应使用毒蕈碱型受体。多数交感靶神经释放去甲肾上腺素，但交感出汗通路使用乙酰胆碱和毒蕈碱型受体。

00:02:02.904 --> 00:02:14.544
Nicotinic receptors also transmit from motor nerves to skeletal muscle. This explains why cholinergic poisoning can cause both secretions and muscle weakness.
烟碱型受体还参与运动神经到骨骼肌的传递，因此胆碱中毒既可分泌增多，也可肌无力。

00:02:14.544 --> 00:02:25.680
These distinctions correct an oversimplified sympathetic-versus-parasympathetic split. Use the receptor effects to predict the breathing and circulation problem you need to manage.
这些区别纠正过于简单的交感与副交感二分法。应从受体效应预测实际需要处理的呼吸及循环问题。

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:38.928
Begin with whether the patient can protect the airway and breathe effectively. Then compare mental status, secretions, skin, pupils, muscle activity, pulse, pressure and temperature.
先判断能否保护气道及有效呼吸，再比较精神状态、分泌、皮肤、瞳孔、肌肉活动、脉搏、血压及温度。

00:02:38.928 --> 00:02:51.096
Dry delirium suggests antimuscarinic effects; wet secretions and weakness suggest cholinergic excess. Sweating with marked arousal suggests a sympathomimetic pattern.
干燥伴谵妄提示抗毒蕈碱效应；分泌旺盛伴无力提示胆碱过量；大量出汗并明显兴奋提示拟交感模式。

00:02:51.096 --> 00:03:03.168
Depressed consciousness with slow, shallow breathing suggests opioid or another depressant effect. Small pupils add evidence but are not a required condition for ventilation support.
意识受抑并呼吸慢浅，提示阿片或其他抑制效应。小瞳孔可增加证据，但支持通气不必等待该条件。

00:03:03.168 --> 00:03:14.232
These are probabilities, not unique chemical fingerprints. An incomplete pattern should increase careful reassessment rather than delay treatment of a visible life threat.
这些是概率线索，不是独一无二的化学指纹。模式不完整时，应加强复评，不能因此延误可见生命威胁的处理。

00:03:14.232 --> 00:03:25.632
Muscarinic blockade reduces normal secretions and can impair sweating. The patient may have dry mouth and skin, flushing, dilated pupils and rising temperature.
毒蕈碱型受体被阻断，会减少正常分泌并可损害出汗；患者可能口皮干、潮红、瞳孔大且温度升高。

00:03:25.632 --> 00:03:37.032
Central effects can include confusion, hallucinations or delirium. A frightened, disoriented patient needs a calm approach and repeated physiological assessment.
中枢效应可包括混乱、幻觉或谵妄。害怕且定向差的患者，需要平静接近和反复生理评估。

00:03:37.032 --> 00:03:48.552
Peripheral effects include tachycardia, urinary retention and reduced bowel activity. Ask about the last normal void and recent medication changes when practical.
外周效应包括心动过速、尿潴留及肠活动减少；可行时应问上次正常排尿和近期药物变化。

00:03:48.552 --> 00:04:01.632
The classic dry-hot-delirious cluster is useful, but no single pupil size, heart rate or skin finding proves the agent. Continue to check glucose, temperature and competing causes.
典型干、热、谵妄组合很有用，但任何单个瞳孔、心率或皮肤发现都不能证明物质种类；仍需查血糖、温度及其他病因。

00:04:01.632 --> 00:04:13.848
Some over-the-counter antihistamines and prescribed medicines have antimuscarinic properties. More than one product can contribute, including combination cold or sleep preparations.
某些非处方抗组胺药及处方药具有抗毒蕈碱作用；多种产品可能共同贡献，包括复方感冒药或助眠制剂。

00:04:13.848 --> 00:04:27.000
Tricyclic antidepressant toxicity also blocks fast cardiac sodium channels. A dry, confused patient can therefore develop conduction delay, seizures and profound hypotension.
三环类抗抑郁药中毒还会阻断心脏快速钠通道，因此干燥混乱者也可能出现传导延迟、抽搐及严重低压。

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:38.160
Look at the rhythm and QRS as well as the skin. A widening complex or deteriorating perfusion is a reason to request advanced support and prepare for rapid decline.
除皮肤外还需观察节律及QRS。波群增宽或灌注恶化，要求取得高级支持并准备应对快速下降。

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:50.712
Current local bicarbonate treatment belongs to an advanced, consultation-led pathway. Recognizing its purpose does not authorize an independent PCP bicarbonate or antiarrhythmic recipe.
现行当地碳酸氢钠处理属于高级、咨询引导路径。理解其目的，并不授权PCP独立实施碳酸氢钠或抗心律失常配方。

00:04:50.712 --> 00:05:02.328
Acetylcholinesterase inhibition can allow acetylcholine to accumulate. Both muscarinic and nicotinic effects may occur, with variable heart rate and pupil findings.
乙酰胆碱酯酶受抑可使乙酰胆碱积聚，同时产生毒蕈碱型及烟碱型效应，心率和瞳孔表现可能不同。

00:05:02.328 --> 00:05:18.312
SLUDGE-M recalls salivation, lacrimation, urination, defecation, gastrointestinal upset, emesis and miosis. Add the three dangerous Bs: bronchorrhea, bronchospasm and bradycardia.
SLUDGE-M提示流涎、流泪、排尿、排便、胃肠不适、呕吐及缩瞳；还需特别记住三项危险B：支气管溢液、痉挛及心动过缓。

00:05:18.312 --> 00:05:31.608
Profuse bronchial secretions and narrowed airways can obstruct effective breathing. Suction and effective ventilation, once contact is safe, matter more than reciting the mnemonic perfectly.
大量支气管分泌和气道收窄可阻碍有效呼吸。安全接触后，吸引及有效通气，比完整背出口诀更重要。

00:05:31.608 --> 00:05:45.048
A wet patient is not automatically a pesticide diagnosis. Pulmonary edema, aspiration and other disease remain possible, and exposure safety must be established before contact.
分泌多不自动确诊农药中毒，还可能有肺水肿、误吸或其他疾病；接触前必须先确认暴露安全。

00:05:45.048 --> 00:05:55.488
Nicotinic overstimulation can progress from twitching to weakness and paralysis. A quieter patient may be losing muscle function rather than recovering.
烟碱型过度刺激可从抽动进展为无力及瘫痪；患者安静下来，可能正在失去肌肉功能，而不是恢复。

00:05:55.488 --> 00:06:07.056
Assess breathing depth, chest movement and air entry, not just a respiratory count. Respiratory muscle failure can coexist with secretions and bronchospasm.
需要评估呼吸深度、胸廓运动和气流，不能只数频率；呼吸肌衰竭可与分泌及支气管痉挛同时存在。

00:06:07.056 --> 00:06:19.824
Atropine reverses muscarinic effects but does not correct the nicotinic muscle problem. The current public J zero five places atropine at ACP and pralidoxime at CCP level.
阿托品可逆转毒蕈碱型效应，却不能纠正烟碱型肌肉问题。当前公开J05把阿托品列为ACP，解磷定列为CCP。

00:06:19.824 --> 00:06:33.672
For an ordinary PCP, the actionable plan is exposure-safe basic support, required consultation and early advanced help. A school phrase saying if in scope does not supply a missing authorization.
普通PCP可行动的是暴露安全的基础支持、所需咨询及及早高级援助。学校“如在权限内”的措辞，不能补足缺少的授权。

00:06:33.672 --> 00:06:45.888
Sympathomimetic agents stimulate adrenergic activity directly or increase catecholamine availability. Examples include cocaine, amphetamines and some other stimulants.
拟交感物质可直接刺激肾上腺素能活动，或增加儿茶酚胺可用量，例如可卡因、苯丙胺及一些其他兴奋剂。

00:06:45.888 --> 00:06:58.704
Agitation, dilated pupils, rapid pulse and high pressure overlap antimuscarinic toxicity. Marked sweating is a useful comparison clue, although mixed exposures can blur it.
激越、瞳孔大、脉快和高压，可与抗毒蕈碱中毒重叠。明显出汗有助比较，但混合暴露可能使区别模糊。

00:06:58.704 --> 00:07:12.264
Danger extends beyond behaviour: assess for chest discomfort, rhythm changes, temperature elevation, seizures and impaired perfusion. Young age does not exclude serious cardiac injury.
危险不限于行为，应评估胸部不适、节律变化、体温升高、抽搐及灌注受损；年轻不能排除严重心脏损伤。

00:07:12.264 --> 00:07:23.592
Sustained muscle activity and heat can contribute to rhabdomyolysis, potassium release and kidney injury. This is one bridge between the two school sections.
持续肌肉活动和热，可促成横纹肌溶解、钾释放及肾损伤，这正是两节学校课程间的一座桥梁。

00:07:23.592 --> 00:07:35.424
Use distance, an exit plan and a calm, simple explanation. Reduce noise and unnecessary confrontation while arranging the resources needed for safe assessment.
保持适当距离及退出计划，用平静简单解释，减少噪声和不必要对抗，并安排安全评估所需资源。

00:07:35.424 --> 00:07:49.920
Agitation can reflect hypoxia, low glucose, infection, neurological disease or heat as well as intoxication. Measure what is safe and immediately useful, including temperature and glucose.
激越可能来自缺氧、低糖、感染、神经疾病、热或中毒，应测安全且立即有用的数据，包括温度和血糖。

00:07:49.920 --> 00:08:03.192
Limit avoidable exertion and use the established heat-illness cooling process when indicated. Do not restrain a patient prone or compromise breathing in order to obtain a tidy set of observations.
应减少可避免用力，有指征时使用既定热病降温流程。不能为取得整齐观察值而俯卧约束或损害呼吸。

00:08:03.192 --> 00:08:16.632
Medication-assisted control requires its actual authorized team and monitoring. Once the patient becomes quieter, immediately reassess airway, ventilation, temperature and perfusion.
药物辅助控制需要真实获准团队及监测。患者一旦安静，必须立即复评气道、通气、温度和灌注。

00:08:16.632 --> 00:08:29.400
Opioid receptor agonism depresses respiratory drive and consciousness. The important observation is whether enough air is reaching the lungs, not simply whether the patient looks asleep.
阿片受体激动会抑制呼吸驱动及意识。关键观察是足够空气是否进入肺部，而不只是患者看起来像睡着。

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:39.576
Count the rate and evaluate depth, air movement and chest rise. Snoring or occasional gasps do not establish adequate ventilation.
要数频率，也评深度、气流及胸廓起伏；鼾声或偶发喘息不证明通气足够。

00:08:39.576 --> 00:08:50.424
Small pupils can support the pattern, but hypoxia, mixed exposure or another condition can change that finding. Do not withhold support while waiting for pinpoint pupils.
小瞳孔可支持该模式，但缺氧、混合暴露或其他状况可改变表现；不能等到针尖样瞳孔才支持。

00:08:50.424 --> 00:09:01.680
Fentanyl-related rigidity can occasionally complicate ventilation. Difficulty ventilating requires prompt troubleshooting and advanced help rather than repeated forceful bagging.
芬太尼相关僵硬有时会使通气困难；难以通气时需及时排查及高级援助，不能只是反复用力挤囊。

00:09:01.680 --> 00:09:13.920
For inadequate breathing with a pulse, establish an open airway, clear secretions and use the indicated adjunct. Obtain a two-provider mask seal when resources allow.
有脉但呼吸不足时，应开放气道、清除分泌并使用有指征辅助物，资源允许时采用双人面罩密封。

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:26.520
Give controlled breaths through the appropriate resuscitation pathway, watching for chest rise and allowing exhalation. Check the mask, position and obstruction before increasing force.
依适当复苏路径给予受控通气，观察胸廓起伏并允许呼气；增加力度前，应先查面罩、体位及阻塞。

00:09:26.520 --> 00:09:38.424
Supplemental oxygen can preserve a saturation reading while carbon dioxide rises from hypoventilation. A reassuring oxygen number cannot replace the breathing examination.
补氧可在低通气造成二氧化碳上升时维持血氧读数，因此放心的氧数值不能代替呼吸检查。

00:09:38.424 --> 00:09:49.584
If there is no definite pulse and the arrest branch applies, prioritize CPR and ventilation. Naloxone must not interrupt the required resuscitation sequence.
若无明确脉搏且符合心搏骤停分支，应优先CPR和通气；纳洛酮不能中断所需复苏顺序。

00:09:49.584 --> 00:10:00.144
Naloxone competitively blocks opioid effects at receptors. Give it for the indicated suspected opioid respiratory problem while effective ventilation continues.
纳洛酮在受体竞争性阻断阿片效应；对有指征的疑似阿片呼吸问题给药，同时继续有效通气。

00:10:00.144 --> 00:10:10.272
The treatment endpoint is adequate spontaneous breathing. Full alertness, anger or withdrawal is not the required sign that the treatment has worked.
治疗目标是恢复足够自主呼吸；完全清醒、愤怒或戒断，并不是证明治疗有效所必需的表现。

00:10:10.272 --> 00:10:20.592
Allow the indicated time for the route to work and reassess before repeating. Count any doses already given by the patient, companions or other responders.
应留出该途径规定起效时间，重复前复评，并计入患者、同行者或其他救援者已给的剂量。

00:10:20.592 --> 00:10:33.840
Palliative and prescribed-opioid cases need careful pain and withdrawal planning with the actual clinical team. Their separate titration instructions must not be blended with a generic overdose schedule.
安宁疗护及处方阿片病例，需要与实际临床团队谨慎安排疼痛及戒断管理；不能把它们独立的滴定指令混入通用过量剂量表。

00:10:33.840 --> 00:10:46.920
The currently checked adult PCP monograph lists point four milligrams, point four, point eight, then two milligrams by the authorized IM or IV route, every three minutes as required.
当前核对的成人PCP专论，依次列出0.4、0.4、0.8，再2毫克，使用获准肌注或静脉途径，按需每三分钟。

00:10:46.920 --> 00:10:59.280
This is not point four repeated four times. The fourth IV dose is preferred in the source, and further doses require CliniCall consultation rather than an improvised continuation.
这不是0.4重复四次。来源对第四剂偏好静脉，之后剂量需CliniCall咨询，不能自行延长。

00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:12.192
Reassess respiratory function and prior treatment at every step. The schedule is a maximum sequence of opportunities, not an instruction to finish every dose after breathing has improved.
每一步都需复评呼吸功能及既往处理。剂量表提供最多四次机会，不是要求呼吸改善后仍把全部剂量给完。

00:11:12.192 --> 00:11:24.168
Verify the actual product concentration and calculate the volume separately. This adult schedule does not supply a neonatal, pediatric, nasal-device or palliative dosing order.
需要另核真实产品浓度并计算体积。这份成人表并不提供新生儿、儿童、鼻喷器或安宁疗护剂量医嘱。

00:11:24.168 --> 00:11:36.312
The current monograph includes a metered intranasal option in the first-responder pathway. A labelled nasal device is not interchangeable with an arbitrary volume from an injectable ampoule.
当前专论在第一救援者路径中包含定量鼻喷选项。标示鼻喷器不能与从注射安瓿任取的体积互换。

00:11:36.312 --> 00:11:48.576
Use the actual supplied device instructions, authorized dose and repeat interval. Do not ask an unresponsive patient to inhale deliberately as a condition for giving a permitted nasal product.
需使用实际器械说明、获准剂量及重复间隔。不能把要求无反应患者主动吸气，当作给予获准鼻喷产品的前提。

00:11:48.576 --> 00:11:59.232
Nasal medication is absorbed through mucosa, while perfusion and local conditions affect delivery. It does not replace assisted ventilation in an apneic patient.
鼻用药经黏膜吸收，灌注及局部状况会影响输送；它不能代替呼吸暂停患者的辅助通气。

00:11:59.232 --> 00:12:10.944
Check whether someone already used a nasal product and at what time. Communicate that treatment as part of the total history rather than resetting the sequence at ambulance arrival.
应查是否已有人用鼻喷产品以及时刻，并把它作为完整治疗史交接，不能救护车到达就把剂量序列重置。

00:12:10.944 --> 00:12:23.592
Sedative-hypnotic drugs and alcohol can reduce awareness, coordination and respiratory function. Pupil findings and circulation vary, especially when several substances are involved.
镇静催眠药和酒精可降低意识、协调及呼吸功能；瞳孔和循环表现各异，混用时尤其如此。

00:12:23.592 --> 00:12:36.600
If breathing improves after naloxone but the patient remains drowsy, continue to protect the airway and investigate other causes. Chasing full consciousness with repeated naloxone can add harm.
纳洛酮后呼吸改善但仍嗜睡时，应继续保护气道并找其他原因；为追求完全清醒而反复加药，可能增加伤害。

00:12:36.600 --> 00:12:50.040
Flumazenil can provoke seizures in selected high-risk or mixed exposures and is a CCP medication in the current local source. It is not a routine PCP response to an unknown sedated patient.
氟马西尼可在某些高危或混合暴露中诱发抽搐，当前当地来源列为CCP药物；它不是PCP处理未知镇静患者的常规反应。

00:12:50.040 --> 00:13:01.944
Maintain a broad differential, including trauma, glucose disturbance, stroke, infection and hypoxia. A substance history should add evidence without closing the assessment.
需保留创伤、血糖异常、中风、感染及缺氧等广泛鉴别；物质史应增加证据，不能终结评估。

00:13:01.944 --> 00:13:15.216
Small pupils with shallow breathing suggest one priority, while small pupils with copious secretions and fasciculations suggest another. In both, breathing support may be immediately necessary.
小瞳孔伴慢浅呼吸，与小瞳孔伴大量分泌及肌束颤动，提示不同模式；但两者都可能立即需要呼吸支持。

00:13:15.216 --> 00:13:27.936
A fast pulse and agitation can also result from low glucose, heat, infection or hypoxia. Measure glucose and temperature and assess actual ventilation and perfusion.
脉快激越也可来自低糖、热、感染或缺氧，因此需测血糖温度，并评真实通气和灌注。

00:13:27.936 --> 00:13:39.048
A reported overdose does not exclude a fall or a stroke. Look for injury, focal findings, last known well and a course that does not fit the proposed explanation.
自述过量不能排除跌倒或中风；要查损伤、局灶表现、最后正常时刻，以及与所提解释不符的病程。

00:13:39.048 --> 00:13:48.888
State the working pattern and the serious alternatives. Then choose actions that address present threats without requiring certainty about the exact chemical.
应说出工作模式及严重替代病因，再选择处理当前威胁的行动，不必先确定确切化学物。

00:13:48.888 --> 00:14:01.296
A chemical exposure is not simply an ordinary medical patient wearing unusual clothing. Residual material can injure responders, contaminate the ambulance and close receiving facilities.
化学暴露并非只是穿着特殊的普通医学患者；残留物可伤救援者、污染车辆，并影响接收机构运作。

00:14:01.296 --> 00:14:15.048
Current J zero one and PR zero five keep BCEHS care out of hot and warm zones and require consultation for exposure and decontamination planning. Do not enter because you recognize the toxidrome.
当前J01及PR05规定BCEHS不在热区或温区照护，并要求暴露及洗消计划咨询；不能因为认出综合征就进入。

00:14:15.048 --> 00:14:28.776
Work with the designated teams on an agent-specific process and confirm appropriate decontamination before loading. Provide clear explanations, privacy, assistance and protection from heat loss.
需与指定团队合作采用物质特定流程，装车前确认适当洗消；提供清楚解释、隐私、协助及防失温措施。

00:14:28.776 --> 00:14:42.072
Do not induce vomiting or improvise neutralization or oral dilution. A caustic ingestion also changes airway choices: the current local source excludes supraglottic devices in that situation.
不能诱导呕吐或自行中和、口服稀释。腐蚀剂摄入还会改变气道选择，当前当地来源对这种情况排除声门上装置。

00:14:42.072 --> 00:14:56.448
Ask what happened using open, nonjudgmental questions. Distinguish accidental dosing error, recreational exposure, occupational exposure and possible intentional self-harm without presuming motivation.
用开放、不评判的问题了解经过，区分意外用药错误、娱乐性暴露、职业暴露及可能故意自伤，但不预设动机。

00:14:56.448 --> 00:15:09.072
Identify the agent, formulation, route and time when possible. A product label or prescribed supply count may help, but missing tablets do not prove that all were swallowed.
尽可能确认物质、剂型、途径和时间。产品标签或处方余量可能有用，但缺少药片不证明全被吞下。

00:15:09.072 --> 00:15:20.472
Use safe information or an appropriate label image rather than carrying a leaking or contaminated container into the ambulance. Do not sniff an unknown substance to identify it.
应使用安全信息或适当标签照片，不能把泄漏或污染容器带入救护车；不得靠嗅闻未知物来鉴定。

00:15:20.472 --> 00:15:33.672
Record observed findings separately from reported history and include previous treatment. Possible self-harm also needs a safe, compassionate mental-health assessment and the appropriate care pathway.
需把观察发现与自述病史分开，并包括既往处理。可能自伤还需要安全、有同情心的精神健康评估及适当照护路径。

00:15:33.672 --> 00:15:47.112
A forty-six-year-old has taken several cold and sleep products and is now confused, flushed and dry. Pupils are large, pulse is one hundred twenty-eight and temperature is thirty-nine point three.
一位46岁者用了多种感冒及助眠产品后混乱、潮红且干燥；瞳孔大、脉128、体温39.3℃。

00:15:47.112 --> 00:15:59.760
The pattern suggests antimuscarinic effects, but the products and amounts remain uncertain. Check glucose, breathing, injury and the medication history rather than diagnosing from dryness alone.
该模式提示抗毒蕈碱效应，但产品及用量仍不明；需查血糖、呼吸、损伤及药史，不能只靠干燥诊断。

00:15:59.760 --> 00:16:11.616
A usable tracing shows a widening QRS. This adds a potentially dangerous cardiac effect and calls for urgent consultation, advanced resources and conveyance.
可用心电图显示QRS增宽，增加危险心脏效应的担忧，要求紧急咨询、高级资源及转运。

00:16:11.616 --> 00:16:22.680
Treat the current physiological threats and heat through the authorized pathway. A later quieter appearance does not establish recovery if ventilation or pressure is worsening.
应依获准路径处理当前生理威胁及热；如果通气或血压恶化，后来安静下来并不证明恢复。

00:16:22.680 --> 00:16:35.136
At a greenhouse spill, the designated team controls the contaminated area. You arrange required consultation and receive the patient only when the contact and decontamination plan is safe.
温室泄漏时，由指定团队控制污染区域；应安排所需咨询，只在接触及洗消计划安全后接收患者。

00:16:35.136 --> 00:16:47.808
The patient has salivation, tearing, wheeze and heavy bronchial secretions, followed by muscle twitching and weak shallow breaths. This fits a concerning cholinergic pattern.
患者流涎、流泪、哮鸣且支气管分泌大量，之后肌肉抽动、呼吸无力浅弱，符合危险胆碱模式。

00:16:47.808 --> 00:16:59.520
After safe access, support airway clearance and effective ventilation while requesting advanced resources. Do not wait for a particular heart rate or every item of SLUDGE-M.
安全接触后，应支持气道清除及有效通气，并取得高级资源；不能等特定心率或SLUDGE-M每项齐全。

00:16:59.520 --> 00:17:11.880
Explain the distinction in handover: secretions threaten airway and airflow, while nicotinic weakness threatens the respiratory pump. Treating one does not guarantee that the other has resolved.
交接需说明区别：分泌威胁气道与气流，烟碱型无力威胁呼吸泵；一项得到处理，不保证另一项已解决。

00:17:11.880 --> 00:17:23.808
A twenty-nine-year-old is unresponsive and breathing shallowly five times per minute. After oxygen is applied, the saturation improves, but chest movement remains poor.
一位29岁者无反应，每分钟仅五次浅呼吸；给氧后血氧改善，但胸廓运动仍差。

00:17:23.808 --> 00:17:35.208
This is still inadequate ventilation. Open and clear the airway, obtain an effective seal and provide assisted breaths while a partner prepares indicated naloxone.
这仍是通气不足。应开放清除气道、取得有效密封并辅助呼吸，同时由搭档准备有指征纳洛酮。

00:17:35.208 --> 00:17:49.296
After treatment, spontaneous depth and rate improve although the patient remains drowsy. Continue monitoring and assess mixed exposure, injury and glucose rather than chasing complete wakefulness.
处理后自主呼吸深度及频率改善，但仍嗜睡；应继续监测并评混合暴露、损伤及血糖，不能只追求完全清醒。

00:17:49.296 --> 00:18:01.800
Plan conveyance and watch for recurrent depression. If the person later declines care, use the actual consent and refusal process rather than calling one response a safe-discharge test.
应安排转运并警惕再次抑制；若之后拒绝照护，需用真实同意拒绝流程，不能把一次反应当成安全离院测试。

00:18:01.800 --> 00:18:13.944
The kidneys filter plasma and then selectively reabsorb or secrete substances along the nephron. Urine is the final output of that regulated process, not a direct copy of the blood.
肾脏滤过血浆，再沿肾单位选择性重吸收或分泌物质；尿液是调节后的最终产物，并不是血液的直接复制。

00:18:13.944 --> 00:18:26.304
Kidneys regulate water, sodium, potassium and acid-base balance. Acute loss of function can therefore produce both retained waste and life-threatening physiological disturbance.
肾脏调节水、钠、钾及酸碱平衡，因此功能急性下降，既可使废物潴留，也可造成致命生理异常。

00:18:26.304 --> 00:18:40.440
Fluid overload can worsen breathing; potassium disturbance can impair cardiac conduction; acidosis can change respiratory demand. Confusion or weakness may be part of the presentation.
液体过多可加重呼吸，钾异常可损心脏传导，酸中毒可改变呼吸需求，混乱或无力也可能是表现。

00:18:40.440 --> 00:18:52.680
Kidney dysfunction can change medicine clearance and adverse-effect risk. A standard dose or familiar pain medicine is not automatically suitable for every patient with suspected injury.
肾功能异常可改变药物清除及不良效应风险，因此标准剂量或熟悉止痛药，并不自动适合每位疑似肾损伤患者。

00:18:52.680 --> 00:19:05.616
Prerenal describes reduced effective perfusion reaching the kidney before primary tissue injury has become the main problem. It is a functional mechanism, not a claim that the patient must look dehydrated.
肾前描述主要肾组织损伤形成前，到达肾脏的有效灌注减少；它是功能机制，不代表患者必须看起来脱水。

00:19:05.616 --> 00:19:18.072
Intrinsic injury affects structures within the kidney, including vessels, glomeruli, tubules or interstitial tissue. Causes include ischemia, inflammation and toxic injury.
肾内损伤影响肾脏内部结构，包括血管、肾小球、肾小管或间质，原因可有缺血、炎症及毒性损伤。

00:19:18.072 --> 00:19:31.344
Postrenal obstruction impedes urine leaving the kidney and can raise pressure upstream. The outflow problem needs identification and definitive relief, not simply more fluid entering the circulation.
肾后阻塞使尿液离开肾脏受阻，并可增加上游压力；需要识别并确定解除引流问题，而不只是往循环输入更多液体。

00:19:31.344 --> 00:19:42.144
These categories can coexist. Prolonged low perfusion can damage tubules, while sepsis may involve both flow abnormalities and intrinsic injury.
这些分类可以并存，持续低灌注可损肾小管，而脓毒症可能同时包含血流异常与肾内损伤。

00:19:42.144 --> 00:19:53.040
Vomiting, diarrhea, hemorrhage and poor intake can reduce circulating volume and renal perfusion. The urine history may add a clue to the wider deterioration.
呕吐、腹泻、出血及摄入少，可减少循环容量和肾灌注；尿量史可增加对全身恶化的线索。

00:19:53.040 --> 00:20:05.448
Sepsis can reduce effective perfusion through tone, leakage and microcirculatory changes. It can also cause intrinsic injury, so one category is not the entire explanation.
脓毒症可通过张力、漏出及微循环变化减少有效灌注，也可造成肾内损伤，因此单一分类并非完整解释。

00:20:05.448 --> 00:20:16.416
Heart failure can impair renal perfusion while edema is present. Low output and congestion make the fluid decision different from uncomplicated volume depletion.
心力衰竭可在已有水肿时损害肾灌注；低心排及淤血使补液决定不同于单纯容量不足。

00:20:16.416 --> 00:20:28.776
A low urine report should prompt assessment of the whole circulation, not an automatic bolus. Early treatment of the cause can prevent prolonged hypoperfusion from becoming structural injury.
尿少报告应促成整体循环评估，不能自动快速补液；及早处理病因，有助避免持续低灌注转为结构损伤。

00:20:28.776 --> 00:20:40.176
Reduced renal perfusion can activate renin release and the angiotensin-aldosterone system. Angiotensin contributes to vasoconstriction and stimulates aldosterone.
肾灌注下降可激活肾素释放及血管紧张素醛固酮系统；血管紧张素参与血管收缩，并刺激醛固酮。

00:20:40.176 --> 00:20:50.664
Aldosterone promotes sodium retention and potassium secretion in appropriate nephron segments, with water balance affected alongside other hormones and intake.
醛固酮促进适当肾单位部位保钠及排钾，水分平衡还同时受其他激素和摄入影响。

00:20:50.664 --> 00:21:03.240
This response helps defend effective circulation but cannot stop hemorrhage, reverse a toxin or remove an obstruction. Preserved pressure may be compensation rather than adequate organ flow.
该反应帮助维持有效循环，却不能止血、逆转毒物或解除阻塞；保住的血压可能来自代偿，而非器官血流足够。

00:21:03.240 --> 00:21:15.624
NSAIDs and renin-angiotensin medicines can alter renal responses during acute illness. Record them for clinical review without instructing the patient to permanently stop a beneficial prescription.
NSAIDs及肾素血管紧张素相关药，可在急病中改变肾反应；应记录供临床复核，不能自行要求患者永久停用有益处方。

00:21:15.624 --> 00:21:27.288
If low perfusion persists, tubular cells can be injured. This is why an initially prerenal problem can develop a structural component rather than staying in one fixed category.
低灌注持续可损伤肾小管细胞，因此最初肾前问题会增加结构损伤，而不是永远固定在同一分类。

00:21:27.288 --> 00:21:41.064
Inflammatory glomerular or interstitial disease and nephrotoxic exposures are other mechanisms. A recent medicine or infection is evidence to explore, not enough to diagnose its exact renal effect.
炎症性肾小球或间质病变及肾毒性暴露也是机制；近期药物或感染是待查证据，尚不足以确定具体肾效应。

00:21:41.064 --> 00:21:54.168
Rhabdomyolysis releases muscle contents, including myoglobin and potassium. Consider prolonged compression, marked heat, seizures or sustained strenuous muscle activity.
横纹肌溶解释放肌肉内容物，包括肌红蛋白及钾；应考虑长期压迫、明显高热、抽搐或持续剧烈肌肉活动。

00:21:54.168 --> 00:22:06.264
Dark urine may reflect pigment, blood, concentration or another cause, and some patients have none. Neither its presence nor absence establishes the diagnosis alone.
深色尿可能来自色素、血、浓缩或其他原因，也有患者并不出现；有无深色尿都不能单独确定诊断。

00:22:06.264 --> 00:22:16.368
Obstruction can occur in the drainage system or at the bladder outlet. Urine backs up and pressure can impair filtration if the problem is significant enough.
阻塞可发生于引流系统或膀胱出口；尿液积聚回压，问题足够严重时可损害滤过。

00:22:16.368 --> 00:22:29.472
For global acute kidney dysfunction, bilateral obstruction, a single functioning kidney or an outlet obstruction is especially relevant. A unilateral stone with a healthy other kidney is a different situation.
全身肾功能急性下降时，双侧阻塞、单个功能肾或出口阻塞尤其相关；单侧结石而另一肾健康，属于不同情况。

00:22:29.472 --> 00:22:43.896
Ask about painful retention, the last normal void and an existing catheter. Observe external drainage or obvious kinking if appropriate, without breaking a closed system or manipulating internal components.
应问疼痛潴留、上次正常排尿及已有导尿管；适当时可看外部引流或明显扭折，但不能破坏封闭系统或操纵内部部件。

00:22:43.896 --> 00:22:57.504
Prompt definitive evaluation may be needed. Do not force oral water or large IV volumes to push urine past a suspected blockage, and do not invent a catheter procedure from the school mechanism lesson.
可能需要及时确定评估；不能强灌水或大量静脉补液，试图把尿推过疑似阻塞，也不能从机制课自创导尿操作。

00:22:57.504 --> 00:23:10.488
The named published KDIGO criteria include a creatinine rise of at least twenty-six point five micromoles per liter within forty-eight hours, or at least one point five times baseline within seven days.
点名已发表KDIGO标准包括：48小时内肌酐增加至少26.5微摩尔每升，或七天内达到基线至少1.5倍。

00:23:10.488 --> 00:23:22.680
Another route is urine output below point five milliliters per kilogram per hour for six hours. These criteria use actual timed data, not a casual report that the patient urinated less.
另一条为尿量低于每公斤每小时0.5毫升、持续六小时；它需要真实计时数据，不能只靠随口说尿少。

00:23:22.680 --> 00:23:34.728
You can suspect kidney risk and act on shock, obstruction or other threats before these laboratory criteria are available. Do not guess a baseline creatinine or wait six hours on scene.
化验标准尚不可得时，也可怀疑肾风险，并处理休克、阻塞等威胁；不能猜基线肌酐，也不能在现场等六小时。

00:23:34.728 --> 00:23:46.344
The official site currently still describes the twenty-twenty-six update as a public-review draft preparing publication. Draft changes are not presented here as an already final replacement.
官方网站目前仍把2026更新描述为公开征求意见后准备发表的草案；本课不会把草案变化说成已定稿替代。

00:23:46.344 --> 00:23:59.544
For a seventy-kilogram patient, point five milliliters per kilogram per hour corresponds to thirty-five milliliters per hour. Over six hours, that rate corresponds to two hundred ten milliliters.
70公斤患者，每公斤每小时0.5毫升对应每小时35毫升；六小时对应210毫升。

00:23:59.544 --> 00:24:10.752
The criterion says below that rate over the required period. A single small void or an incompletely emptied collection bag does not establish the measured six-hour total.
标准要求在规定期间低于该速率；一次少量排尿，或未完整处理的收集袋，不能确定六小时实测总量。

00:24:10.752 --> 00:24:24.912
Check the start and finish times, measured amount, estimated mass and whether collection was complete. If any are uncertain, communicate that uncertainty instead of creating a precise diagnosis.
应核起止时刻、测得尿量、估计体重及收集是否完整；任一不确定，都应说明，而不是制造精确诊断。

00:24:24.912 --> 00:24:37.296
A normal urine volume does not exclude AKI through the creatinine pathway. Likewise, an oliguric patient does not automatically need an extra two hundred ten milliliters of fluid.
尿量正常不能排除通过肌酐路径达到的AKI；同样，少尿也不自动意味着需要额外输入210毫升液体。

00:24:37.296 --> 00:24:47.136
In this paper exercise, verified results show creatinine rising from eighty-four to one hundred twelve micromoles per liter within forty-eight hours.
本纸面练习有已核实结果：48小时内，肌酐从84升至112微摩尔每升。

00:24:47.136 --> 00:24:59.520
The increase is twenty-eight, which exceeds twenty-six point five. The ratio is about one point three three, so the relative one-point-five route is not needed to meet the absolute-change criterion.
增幅为28，高于26.5；比值约1.33，因此即使未达1.5倍，也可通过绝对变化条件。

00:24:59.520 --> 00:25:12.768
The criteria are alternatives, not three mandatory boxes. Use the actual timing, units and clinical context, and distinguish a verified laboratory record from a patient recollection.
这些条件是替代路径，不是三项必须同时符合；需使用真实时刻、单位及临床背景，并区分核实化验与患者回忆。

00:25:12.768 --> 00:25:24.144
This is interpretation practice, not permission to claim a field laboratory diagnosis without data. Current symptoms and the reason for the change still need assessment.
这里练的是解释能力，不代表没有数据也可宣称现场化验诊断；当前症状和变化原因仍需评估。

00:25:24.144 --> 00:25:34.152
Establish what is normal for this patient: known kidney disease, usual urine production, prescribed fluid limits and dialysis schedule when relevant.
应先建立本人基线：已知肾病、平常尿量、处方液体限制，以及相关时的透析计划。

00:25:34.152 --> 00:25:45.936
Ask about vomiting, diarrhea, bleeding, poor intake, urinary difficulty, fever and new pain. The reason for reduced urine may sit outside the kidneys.
需问呕吐、腹泻、出血、摄入少、排尿困难、发热及新疼痛；尿少原因可能在肾脏之外。

00:25:45.936 --> 00:25:58.800
Review new prescriptions, over-the-counter NSAIDs, diuretics, potassium-containing supplements and recent exposures. Record the timing and actual product rather than only the label kidney medicine.
应复核新处方、非处方NSAIDs、利尿剂、含钾补充品及近期暴露，记录时间与实际产品，而不只写“肾药”。

00:25:58.800 --> 00:26:11.376
Breathlessness, swelling, generalized weakness, palpitations or confusion can signal complications. None is specific, so assess the whole patient and consider alternatives.
气促、水肿、全身无力、心悸或混乱可提示并发症，但都不特异，因此需整体评估并考虑替代病因。

00:26:11.376 --> 00:26:23.880
A dehydrated patient with gastrointestinal losses may benefit from indicated, carefully reassessed volume support. A congested patient with weak cardiac output needs a different assessment.
胃肠丢失的脱水者，可能从有指征且谨慎复评的容量支持获益；心排差的淤血患者则需要不同评估。

00:26:23.880 --> 00:26:37.776
Edema and poor perfusion can coexist. Listen to breathing, assess work and oxygenation, examine the circulation and compare the history rather than classifying volume from swollen ankles alone.
水肿与低灌注可以并存；应查呼吸音、功和氧合，评循环并比较病史，不能只从踝肿分类容量。

00:26:37.776 --> 00:26:47.592
A blocked outlet may explain little urine without simple total-body dehydration. More fluid cannot substitute for relief of the drainage problem.
出口阻塞可在并非单纯全身脱水时造成尿少；更多液体不能替代解除引流问题。

00:26:47.592 --> 00:26:59.304
The useful question is which mechanism is most likely and which finding would change the plan. Multiple mechanisms or poor response are reasons for consultation and reassessment.
有用的问题是哪个机制最可能、什么发现会改变计划；多机制或反应差时，应咨询并复评。

00:26:59.304 --> 00:27:11.448
Use vascular access and fluids only when indicated through the actual local pathway. Establish the baseline and the response you expect, such as improved perfusion without worsening breathing.
静脉通路和液体必须经真实当地路径具备指征；先建立基线及预期反应，例如灌注改善但呼吸不恶化。

00:27:11.448 --> 00:27:22.872
Administer the permitted amount and rate, then reassess. A low urine report does not authorize an unlimited bolus or require completion of a whole bag before transport.
按获准量及速率给予后复评；尿少报告不能授权无限快速补液，也不要求转运前先输完整袋。

00:27:22.872 --> 00:27:37.176
Worsening air movement, work of breathing, oxygenation or congestion requires prompt review alongside the circulation. Failure to improve pressure is not proof that another identical bolus is correct.
气流、呼吸功、氧合或淤血恶化时，需与循环一起及时复核；血压未改善，不证明再来一份同样快速补液就是正确。

00:27:37.176 --> 00:27:49.848
Do not independently prescribe a diuretic, stop all long-term medicines or operate dialysis equipment from a general textbook table. Coordinate definitive care and protect continuity.
不能从一般教材表独立开利尿剂、停全部长期药或操作透析设备；应协调确定照护并保护连续性。

00:27:49.848 --> 00:28:02.784
Reduced renal excretion, muscle breakdown and shifts across cell membranes can increase extracellular potassium. Ask about dialysis, medicines, tissue injury and the actual course.
肾排泄减少、肌肉分解及跨细胞移动，都可升高细胞外钾；应问透析、药物、组织损伤及真实病程。

00:28:02.784 --> 00:28:14.952
Generalized weakness and abnormal rhythms may be warning signs, but symptoms are often nonspecific. The laboratory confirms the concentration when appropriate testing is available.
全身无力和异常节律可能是警讯，但症状常不特异；适当检测可得时，由化验确定浓度。

00:28:14.952 --> 00:28:28.992
Possible ECG clues include tented T waves, small or absent P waves, a long PR and wide or bizarre complexes, including bradycardia. Do not infer a precise potassium from one waveform.
心电线索可有尖帐篷样T、小或消失P、PR延长、宽或怪异波群，甚至心动过缓；不能从单个波形推算精确钾值。

00:28:28.992 --> 00:28:41.544
A normal-looking ECG does not exclude dangerous hyperkalemia, and the changes need not follow a fixed staircase. Clinical context and deterioration still require urgent evaluation.
看似正常心电图不能排除危险高钾，变化也不一定按固定阶梯出现；临床背景及恶化仍需紧急评估。

00:28:41.544 --> 00:28:51.768
The treatment categories have different purposes. Calcium protects the myocardium against potassium effects, but it does not remove potassium from the body.
各治疗类别目的不同：钙保护心肌抵抗钾效应，但并不把钾从身体排出。

00:28:51.768 --> 00:29:03.648
Insulin-based or selected other therapies can shift potassium into cells temporarily. Definitive removal may require dialysis or another clinician-selected elimination approach.
胰岛素相关或某些其他疗法可暂时把钾移入细胞；确定移除可能需要透析或临床选择的其他排出方式。

00:29:03.648 --> 00:29:18.528
The current E zero three advanced pathway requires significant instability, a compatible suspicion and consultation. A PCP bronchodilator permission is not independent permission for a potassium-shifting dose.
当前E03高级路径需要显著不稳定、相符怀疑及咨询；PCP支气管扩张药权限，不等于独立给予移钾剂量的权限。

00:29:18.528 --> 00:29:32.832
At PCP level, address current airway and breathing needs, monitor, obtain indicated access and arrange urgent advanced and definitive care. Give a clear warning about the suspected mechanism and rhythm.
PCP当前应处理气道呼吸需求、监测、取得有指征通路，并安排紧急高级及确定照护，清楚预警疑似机制及节律。

00:29:32.832 --> 00:29:43.896
A seventy-two-year-old with known heart failure and kidney disease reports much less urine. Breathlessness and ankle swelling have increased, and peripheral perfusion is poor.
一位72岁心衰及肾病患者表示尿量明显减少，气促和踝肿增加，同时外周灌注差。

00:29:43.896 --> 00:29:55.080
Do not label this simple dehydration from the urine report. Low effective output and congestion can coexist, while obstruction or another acute illness may add.
不能因尿少就贴上单纯脱水标签；低有效心排及淤血可以并存，也可能增加阻塞或其他急病。

00:29:55.080 --> 00:30:09.720
Assess breathing and circulation, obtain useful rhythm information, check glucose and ask about medicines, urinary symptoms and baseline care. Consider potassium risk without assuming a concentration.
应评呼吸循环、取得有用节律、查血糖，并问药物、泌尿症状及基线照护；考虑钾风险但不猜浓度。

00:30:09.720 --> 00:30:20.736
Provide indicated support and seek an individualized care plan and conveyance. A routine large fluid bolus or automatic drug bundle could worsen this patient.
需提供有指征支持，取得个体化计划并转运；常规大量快速补液或自动整套药物，可能使其恶化。

00:30:20.736 --> 00:30:32.952
A thirty-four-year-old has had prolonged agitation and heavy muscle activity. Now there is marked heat, muscle pain and a report of dark urine followed by much less output.
一位34岁者长时间激越并剧烈肌肉活动，现在明显发热、肌痛，自述先深色尿、后尿量明显减少。

00:30:32.952 --> 00:30:45.192
Possible mechanisms include fluid loss, muscle breakdown and kidney injury. Dark urine supports concern but does not prove myoglobin, and the exact exposure remains uncertain.
可能机制包括液体丢失、肌肉分解及肾损伤；深色尿增加担忧，却不能证明肌红蛋白，确切暴露仍不明。

00:30:45.192 --> 00:30:58.032
Continue safety, temperature management, breathing and circulation support while arranging urgent evaluation. Assess rhythm and glucose and anticipate potassium-related deterioration.
应继续安全、温度管理及呼吸循环支持，安排紧急评估；查节律及血糖，并预期钾相关恶化。

00:30:58.032 --> 00:31:09.816
Communicate the sequence rather than only the word intoxicated. The receiving team needs the duration, heat, muscle findings, urine change, measured observations and response.
交接应传达顺序，而不只写“中毒”；接收团队需要持续时间、热、肌肉发现、尿量变化、实测观察及反应。

00:31:09.816 --> 00:31:22.032
Reassessment begins with function. After airway support or naloxone, check spontaneous depth and rate, air entry, oxygenation and the need for ongoing assistance.
复评从功能开始：气道支持或纳洛酮后，应查自主呼吸深度频率、气流、氧合及是否仍需辅助。

00:31:22.032 --> 00:31:32.928
After volume or positioning actions, compare perfusion and breathing with the recorded baseline. A better pressure alone cannot outweigh worsening respiratory function.
容量或体位处理后，要与记录基线比较灌注及呼吸；单是血压变好，不能抵消呼吸功能恶化。

00:31:32.928 --> 00:31:45.360
Repeat relevant secretion, muscle, temperature and urine-history checks. Some changes occur slowly, so use the actual timeline instead of promising immediate renal recovery.
应重复相关分泌、肌肉、温度及尿史核查；部分变化较慢，因此需用真实时间线，不能保证肾功能立即恢复。

00:31:45.360 --> 00:31:57.576
If the predicted response does not occur, reconsider delivery failure, co-exposure and another diagnosis. Update the receiving team when the urgency or care requirement changes.
预期反应未出现时，需重想输送失败、共同暴露及其他诊断；紧迫性或照护需要变化时，要更新接收团队。

00:31:57.576 --> 00:32:08.616
Start with the current threat: inadequate ventilation, a contaminated exposure, a widening-complex rhythm, severe heat or suspected renal deterioration.
先说当前威胁：通气不足、污染暴露、波群增宽节律、严重热病，或疑似肾功能恶化。

00:32:08.616 --> 00:32:19.008
Add the exposure and timeline or renal baseline and urine history. Separate a measured result, a witness report and an inference about the mechanism.
再加暴露及时间线，或肾基线及尿史；区分实测结果、目击报告与机制推断。

00:32:19.008 --> 00:32:30.000
Report exactly what was delivered, including prior responders, route, dose, time and ventilation support. Then describe the actual change and remaining problem.
准确报告已提供处理，包括先前救援者、途径、剂量、时刻及通气支持，再说明实际变化和剩余问题。

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:43.176
Use working terms such as suspected opioid effect with persistent sedation or possible mixed renal mechanisms. Clear uncertainty is more useful than an unsupported definitive diagnosis.
可使用“疑似阿片效应但仍镇静”或“可能混合肾机制”等工作用语；清楚不确定性，比没有依据的确定诊断更有用。

00:32:43.176 --> 00:32:54.936
Explain why a wet, weak patient and a dry, delirious patient suggest different receptor effects. Include the breathing threat and a competing cause for each.
应解释分泌多且无力，与干燥谵妄为何提示不同受体效应；各自加入呼吸威胁及一种竞争病因。

00:32:54.936 --> 00:33:04.560
Next explain the three renal categories using one cause each, then show how prolonged hypoperfusion or sepsis can combine categories.
接着为三种肾分类各举一个原因，再说明持续低灌注或脓毒症如何使分类并存。

00:33:04.560 --> 00:33:15.264
For an original case, say your immediate safe action, the authorization check and the response you expect. Do not answer only with the drug or disease name.
对原创病例，应说即时安全行动、授权核查及预期反应，不能只报药名或病名。

00:33:15.264 --> 00:33:28.488
Finally state what would make you revise the plan, such as inadequate ventilation, a widening rhythm, rising respiratory work or an exposure hazard. This makes the explanation clinically usable.
最后说会促使修订计划的发现，例如通气不足、波群增宽、呼吸功上升或暴露危险，让解释真正能用于临床。

00:33:28.488 --> 00:33:37.872
You should now compare the school toxidromes through secretions, mental status, breathing, pupils, muscle effects, circulation and temperature.
现在应能通过分泌、精神状态、呼吸、瞳孔、肌肉效应、循环及温度，比较学校各中毒综合征。

00:33:37.872 --> 00:33:48.264
You should explain why ventilation cannot wait for naloxone, why adequate breathing is the endpoint and why contamination requires a separate safe-access plan.
应能解释通气为何不能等待纳洛酮、足够呼吸为何是终点，以及污染为何需要独立安全接触计划。

00:33:48.264 --> 00:34:01.656
For AKI, explain the three mechanisms, interpret genuine urine and creatinine data, and recognize volume, potassium and acid-base consequences without inventing treatment authority.
对于AKI，应解释三机制、解读真实尿量肌酐数据，并在不自创治疗权限的前提下识别容量、钾及酸碱后果。

00:34:01.656 --> 00:34:12.768
Use the bilingual readings to review the mechanisms, then rehearse the original cases aloud. Return to the missed mechanism when an answer is only a memorized label.
使用中英阅读复习机制，再口头排练原创病例；答案若只有背熟标签，就应回到漏掉的机制。
